    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Up8DP7YiKzjdSHvkNw1nt2)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; builds on merged #454, #460, #472, #478, #479\n- Depends on: nothing open\n- If merged first: nothing breaks\n- Conflicts with: none of the open PRs (#443, #455 touch `sp-devonthink-*`, not `sp-fetch-inbox`)\n- After merging: nothing to retarget\n- Branch name is not number-prefixed (`claude/project-thread-47akys`): GitHub branch rename is blocked from cloud sessions; rename by hand if you want it (PR is #539)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Sia's ask, read as: replace a PDF \"if needed\" (better or corrected copy of an article already filed) and refile it in DEVONthink.\n- New flow in `sp-fetch-inbox`:\n  - open the new copy from the inbox; press `C-c C-p` (`sp-fetch-inbox-replace`) and pick an existing key, or type that key\n  - `C-c C-c`: when the key is in a `.bib` and `KEY.pdf` exists, filing becomes a replacement (before: error \"already exists\")\n  - confirmation names the file, the backup folder and the key; nothing changes before yes\n- Replacement:\n  - old file copied to `sp-fetch-inbox-backup-dir` (default `~/Documents/literature/replaced/`) as `KEY-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.pdf`\n  - new PDF overwrites `KEY.pdf`\n  - existing `.bib` entry is kept: nothing appended, so citekey and litnote links stay\n- DEVONthink:\n  - record whose file is `KEY.pdf` (looked up by path) is kept, so UUID, tags, metadata and links stay and no duplicate appears\n  - record of the new copy (inbox) is moved to the DEVONthink trash (restorable)\n  - no record for `KEY.pdf`: new file is indexed, as usual\n- Assumptions:\n  - \"refile\" means keep the existing record and swap the file under it, not create a second record\n  - undo = the backup copy plus the DEVONthink trash\n  - highlights DEVONthink stored inside the old file are in the backup, not the new file\n  - metadata sync is skipped (the entry is unchanged)\n- Docs: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-fetch-inbox.org` (\"Replacing a PDF\", bullet lists); `tools/check-tangle.sh` shows only the expected tangle of this doc. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n- Tests: 37/37 ERT pass in Emacs 29 with DEVONthink faked (5 new).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Put a copy of an article in `inbox/`, `M-x sp-fetch-inbox`, pick it, press `C-c C-p`, choose an existing key: header hint says `will replace KEY.pdf` (untested by Claude, GUI)\n- [ ] `C-c C-c`, answer `n`: nothing changes (file, backup folder, DEVONthink)\n- [ ] `C-c C-c`, answer `y`: `KEY.pdf` is the new file, `~/Documents/literature/replaced/KEY-<time>.pdf` is the old one, `.bib` entry unchanged and not duplicated\n- [ ] DEVONthink (untested by Claude): the record of `KEY.pdf` keeps its UUID/tags, shows the new content, inbox record is in the trash\n- [ ] DEVONthink, indexed inbox record and imported inbox record both work (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Edge: a key in a `.bib` with no `KEY.pdf` still errors; `KEY.pdf` with no entry still errors\n- [ ] Regression: filing a normal new article (new key) still moves the PDF, renames the record and appends the entry\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/project-thread-47akys`; remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- Undo a test replacement: copy the file in `~/Documents/literature/replaced/` back over `KEY.pdf`, and restore the inbox record from the DEVONthink trash.\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9DXQMMjFEdMfVcshS)_",
